00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.400
The demand for citizen
developers is on the rise,

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.260
with an estimated
2 billion people

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.420
who can benefit
from this skill set.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.450
But what exactly is
a citizen developer?

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.460
In short, they're are
the people closest

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:32.310
to the problem who've been
empowered to find or create

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:33.630
a solution.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:36.120
In order for these
individuals to be empowered,

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.890
they need access
to technology that

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.440
is democratized in
nature while preventing

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.560
the use of non-IT-sanctioned
third party platforms,

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.530
also known as shadow IT.

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:51.240
Google Cloud's no-code platform
AppSheet provides just that.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.640
It allows anyone the
access and ability

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.310
to create applications
within the framework provided

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:57.870
by their IT team.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.600
Let's walk through
a quick example.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:04.709
Meet Annie, an operational lead
for a manufacturing company.

00:01:04.709 --> 00:01:06.360
Annie has been
receiving feedback

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.820
that the current inspection
practice is inefficient

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:11.220
and impacting the
customer experience.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.040
Workers want a mobile
solution, but her IT team

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.920
doesn't have the time
to build an application.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:20.730
She needs something custom and
she needs to find it quickly.

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.310
Annie discovers AppSheet,
a no-code platform

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:26.430
that can help her create an
application in days or weeks,

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:28.740
rather than months or years.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.210
When working with
the platform, she

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.610
discovers that there are
governance capabilities

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.710
and she's able to
work with her IT team

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:36.570
to put the right
policies in place that

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.760
can prevent shadow IT.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:40.590
She builds an app
within this framework

00:01:40.590 --> 00:01:42.000
and shares it with
her colleagues

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.820
on the manufacturing floor,
iterating with feedback

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:48.000
until she's built the right
solution for the need.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.710
Not only has Annie
helped her team,

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:52.320
but she's obtained the valuable
skill set of building apps

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.860
with no-code.

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:56.550
This means that in addition
to being an operations lead,

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:58.560
she can now count
herself among the growing

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.720
group of citizen developers.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.520
Other departments
soon take notice

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:06.150
of how quickly Annie was able to
solve the problem with no-code.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:09.300
Since IT has already provided
governance guidelines,

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:12.180
other teams are able to start
leveraging AppSheet, becoming

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.760
citizen developers themselves.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:16.680
And it's not just
operations leaders

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.750
who benefit from
citizen development.

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:21.360
Accountants, teachers,
IT professionals,

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.510
and more have all enlisted
no-code technology to digitally

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:28.110
transform their work with custom
line of business solutions,

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:29.520
like Annie's.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.890
Ready to start your
citizen developer journey?

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:34.440
Get started today by clicking
the link in the description

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:35.290
